import SAP.P045b.Defs

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option relaxedAutoImplicit false

/-- P045-T17; pp. 297–299 (PDF pp. 9–11).
Empty realized HT cells contribute zero without being discarded; unconditional and nonempty-event conditional expectations have the stated identities, while empty Hajek ratios and ordinary sample means for realized exposure cells are undefined. -/
theorem SAP.P045b.T17 : SAP.P045b.T17Statement := by sorry

/-- P045-T18; p. 292 (PDF p. 4).
Ordered coordinate removal ignores own treatment and gives a bijective reindexing with a unique outcome function and the four-coordinate example. -/
theorem SAP.P045b.T18 : SAP.P045b.T18Statement := by sorry

/-- P045-T19; pp. 309–310 (PDF pp. 21–22).
With a fixed treated count, treated peers number K minus own treatment, giving the corrected saturation formula and the three-member example. -/
theorem SAP.P045b.T19 : SAP.P045b.T19Statement := by sorry

/-- P045-T20; p. 305 (PDF p. 17).
On the nine-vertex path no set satisfies the literal pairwise-within-three reading and the covering clause, whereas exactly the thirteen listed sets satisfy the corrected separation reading. -/
theorem SAP.P045b.T20 : SAP.P045b.T20Statement := by sorry

/-- P045-T21; p. 305 (PDF p. 17).
Corrected epsilon-nets are maximal separated sets, exist by the bounded finite greedy construction, and have exactly the thirteen listed instances on the nine-vertex path. -/
theorem SAP.P045b.T21 : SAP.P045b.T21Statement := by sorry

/-- P045-T22; pp. 299–300 (PDF pp. 11–12).
The fair-sign witness has exact mean-SE agreement and positive variance-estimate bias but fails relative consistency, while its point estimate and absolute variance error are consistent.
This is the audit witness, rather than either estimator in Table 16.1. -/
theorem SAP.P045b.T22 : SAP.P045b.T22Statement := by sorry

/-- P045-T23; pp. 299–300 (PDF pp. 11–12), Table 16.1.
The six table ratios have the corrected finite-sample comparisons; the witness, the vanishing-variance implication, the nonvanishing-variance counterexample, and the mean-square inequality delimit what mean-SE agreement implies. -/
theorem SAP.P045b.T23 : SAP.P045b.T23Statement := by sorry

/-- P045-T24; p. 312 (PDF p. 24), Figure 16.6; model on p. 310.
The dilated model gives the five effect formulas and the ordering and ratio of direct effects, and total equals direct at psi plus indirect for every outcome schedule. -/
theorem SAP.P045b.T24 : SAP.P045b.T24Statement := by sorry

